messages:
maria: heads-up — several customers hit runtime errors when using the JS SDK in edge functions. stack traces point to fetch/undici shimming and ESM/CJS import failures. any guidance we can publish for the SDK + sample apps?
chris: which runtimes specifically? node versions vs workers?
maria: reported on Vercel Edge (isomorphic env), Cloudflare Workers, node 16 Lambda, node 18+ containers, and bun in one case. errors vary: "Cannot use import statement outside a module" or undici v5 ESM-only errors in CJS apps, and type errors for fetch in TS.
sam: TL;DR we should stop forcing undici as the default runtime fetch. recommendation: runtime detection + lazy dynamic import fallback. publish a short doc: "Edge: use global fetch; Node: prefer global fetch if available, otherwise dynamically import undici; CJS clients: avoid static import of undici v5 (ESM-only)."
leo: +1. Also add a small TypeScript snippet showing how to get a typed fetch without forcing lib: [explain tsconfig caveats]. many folks forget to set "lib": ["DOM"] for browser/edge emulation which gives fetch types. for node-only packages maybe document enabling "es2022" libs and adding "skipLibCheck": true if necessary.
maria: can we craft a micro-snippet for the SDK repo and for sample-apps? something tiny we can paste in Quickstart.
sam: here's a pragmatic pattern (works in ESM; for CJS we have to wrap in an async function):
```js
// lib/getFetch.js (ESM)
let _fetch;
export async function getFetch() {
  if (_fetch) return _fetch;
  if (typeof globalThis.fetch === 'function') {
    _fetch = globalThis.fetch;
    return _fetch;
  }
  // undici v5 is ESM-only; dynamic import avoids require-time errors in CJS consumers
  const undici = await import('undici');
  _fetch = undici.fetch;
  return _fetch;
}

// usage
const fetch = await getFetch();
const res = await fetch(url, opts);
```
leo: for CJS quickstart we can provide a wrapper that uses dynamic import via `import('undici')` inside an async function — but note top-level await isn't available in CJS. show a small helper: `const {getFetch} = require('./lib/getFetch.cjs')` where the file returns a promise for fetch.
chris: packaging notes: mark undici as an optionalDependency or peerDependency? I think optionalDependency is safer so customers who already have a fetch polyfill don’t get duplicate installs. if undici is a peerDep we push the burden on users. also mention bundlers — bundling undici into browser/edge builds is a no-op and will bloat bundles.
sam: agree: optionalDependency + runtime dynamic import. plus in our published ESM build exports, avoid tree-shaking static `import 'undici'` at module scope. keep imports local to functions.
maria: typing guidance for TS quickstart?
leo: short checklist for the doc: 
- Edge runtimes (Cloudflare, Vercel Edge, Denoish): rely on global fetch; do NOT ship undici or polyfills by default.
- Node 18+: has global fetch; prefer it. suggest using the global if present.
- Node <18: recommend optional undici fallback. provide `npm i undici` example.
- CJS consumers: show a tiny adapter file so they don't hit ESM-only import errors.
- TS: if consuming in browser/edge (or libs targeting DOM), set tsconfig lib to include "DOM" so fetch types exist; otherwise include `@types/node` / target Node types and mention "dom" lib may conflict in some lib targets; show `skipLibCheck` workaround if needed.

Add this bit about bundlers and detection: many bundlers will inline `import('undici')` calls at build time unless the import specifier is dynamic or the code path is clearly conditional. recommend using a runtime string for the specifier in docs: `await import(process.env.NODE_ENV ? 'undici' : 'undici')` (yes silly, but bundlers treat it differently) or add bundler ignore comments. note: risky — document as advanced tip only.
chris: can someone open a small PR to: update SDK code with getFetch helper, add Quickstart snippet, and update sample-apps to remove static undici import? test matrix: node16 (no fetch), node18+, vercel-edge, cf-workers.
maria: I can own the PR and tests. sam pls draft the doc blurb, leo pls add TS notes + example tsconfig. i'll file the issue.
devex-bot: Created issue #1897: "SDK: fetch runtime detection + polyfill guidance" assigned to maria, linked to sample-apps PR draft. :rocket:
maria: thanks — will ping once I have a draft. we'll include a small migration note in the changelog so customers upgrading from older SDKs know why they may need to `npm i undici` on Node 16. :thumbsup:
